    a: 'Eight. Each cell holds exactly one card, so you have eight temporary parking spaces in total — twice as many as FreeCell. Four of them start the game already filled with the four cards left over after the deal; the other four start empty and ready to use.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is Eight Off different from FreeCell?',
    a: 'Two things. First, the tableau builds down in suit, not down in alternating colours — a Six of Hearts only goes on a Seven of Hearts. Second, there are eight free cells instead of four, with four of them pre-filled at the deal. The extra cells make Eight Off more forgiving even though the same-suit rule is stricter.',
  },
